   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- `fieldnotes/cli.py:21` prints `note['created']` as it is stored, with no reformatting.\n- `fieldnotes/store.py:24` writes that value with `moment.isoformat()`. This gives strings like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`, using UTC.\n- Nothing else in the code formats dates. `add` prints only the note text, and there is no `strftime` or locale formatting anywhere.\n\nThe format depends on what is stored. If `notes.json` already holds entries written some other way, `list` would print them unchanged. Everything written through `store.add` is ISO-8601.\n\nI didn't change any files. I also didn't open `tools/check.py`. Your grep for date-related terms didn't match it.",
