   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`, which prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note. `python tools/check.py` passes: both tests are OK and no lines are over 100 characters.\n\n- **Date format:** Notes store a full ISO timestamp, so `DATE` is just the date part, for example `2026-01-02: first`. If you'd rather print the whole timestamp, change `[:10]` in the `export` branch of `fieldnotes/cli.py`.\n- **Usage message:** I updated it in `fieldnotes/cli.py` to mention `export`.\n- **Test:** The new test is `tests/test_cli.py`. It adds two notes and checks the exported lines.\n- **Running the checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` to be set. I pointed it at a fresh temp directory for the run.",
